 for this program.","picks":["CRIM B1","CRIM B2","CRIM B3"],"total":{"max":34,"min":31},"up_to":9.0},"gaps":[{"coci":[{"code":"SOCI B2","current_ccn":null,"program_ccn":"CCC000291569","status":"Active"}],"kind":"Catalog and state file differ","owner":"college","text":"The state''s Program Course File lists SOCI B2; the reader found it not in the text. The program points at SOCI B2 CCC000291569, Active in COCI.","where":"Bakersfield College''s program record in the state''s curriculum inventory"},{"coci":[{"code":"SOCI B36","current_ccn":null,"program_ccn":"CCC000240131","status":"Active"}],"kind":"Catalog and state file differ","owner":"college","text":"The state''s Program Course File lists SOCI B36; the reader found it not in the text. The program points at SOCI B36 CCC000240131, Active in COCI.","where":"Bakersfield College''s program record in the state''s curriculum inventory"},{"coci":[{"code":"SOCI B45","current_ccn":null,"program_ccn":"CCC000302335","status":"Active"}],"kind":"Catalog and state file differ","owner":"college","text":"The state''s Program Course File lists SOCI B45; the reader found it not in the text; catalog prints ETHN B45 ''Sociology of Race and Ethnicity'' (same title) in Area 6, recorded as a catalog addition. The program points at SOCI B45 CCC000302335, Active in COCI.","where":"Bakersfield College''s program record in the state''s curriculum inventory"},{"coci":[{"code":"ETHN B45","current_ccn":null,"program_ccn":"CCC000623380","status":"Inactive"}],"kind":"Catalog and state file differ","owner":"college","text":"The catalog prints ETHN B45 for this program, and the state''s Program Course File carries it there: the program points at ETHN B45 CCC000623380, Inactive in COCI.","where":"Bakersfield College''s program record in the state''s curriculum inventory"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"The catalog prints codes run together without a space (e.g. ''ADMJB40''); they are recorded with a space between subject and number to match the Program Course File format.","where":"Bakersfield College''s eLumen reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"Core Courses heading states a total of 25-28 units; it contains the blocks Understanding the Law through American Government. Overall program total stated as 31-34.","where":"Bakersfield College''s eLumen reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"Ethics and American Government each list a single course under ''Complete the following number of credits: 3''; recorded as ''all''.","where":"Bakersfield College''s eLumen reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"List A is recorded as one block: the student selects two courses (6 units) from two different areas, one course per area. Areas: Area 1 Administrative of Justice/Criminology (CRIM B1, B2, B3, B4, B5, B9, B21); Area 2 Business (BSAD B18); Area 3 Economics (ECON C2001, C2002); Area 4 Political Science (POLS B2, B3, B4); Area 5 Public Policy (CRIM B6, JRNL B5, PBHS B22, PBHS B23, SOCI B1); Area 6 Diversity (ANTH B2, COMM B6, GEOG B2, SOCI B28, ETHN B45). Each area printed ''Total 3''. Courses used in the core may not be reused in List A.","where":"Bakersfield College''s eLumen reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"COMM B5 and COMM B15 appear in both Oral Communication and Critical Thinking; CRIM B1, B2, B4 and BSAD B18 appear in both Understanding the Law and List A.","where":"Bakersfield College''s eLumen reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"ETHN B45 is not in the closed list; the closed list has SOCI B45 with the same title, possibly a renumbering—reviewer should check.","where":"Bakersfield College''s eLumen reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"The description names transfer majors (Political Science, Communication Studies, Economics, Philosophy, Social and Behavioral Sciences), not careers, so careers is empty.","where":"Bakersfield College''s eLumen reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"The 60-unit degree total and CalGETC are general degree requirements, not part of the major total.","where":"Bakersfield College''s eLumen reading procedure"}],"map":{"checked_run":"college-page-read run 37810652946","host":"programmap.bakersfieldcollege.edu","status":"refused","text":"programmap.bakersfieldcollege.edu answered 403 Forbidden to the CPL Initiative''s reader on 2026-10-08 (one load), as every Program Mapper host read so far has: the refusal is the mapper service''s. The college''s own Program Pathways Mapper page answers and says each program shows a semester-by-semester path. The reader keeps its name and never retries a refusal another way. It looks for the sequence on the college''s own pages and in its catalog (Sam, open-asks sheet 29 card 3, 2026-10-04).","url":"https://www.bakersfieldcollege.edu/academics/program-mapper.html"},"v":1}'::jsonb from public.program_requirement_records r where r.college = 'Bakersfield College' and r.control_number = '42226' on conflict (college, control_number) do update set display = excluded.display;
