 18 units.","where":"Moreno Valley College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"Requirement: 18 units of study across three disciplines, 9 units of which must be in a single discipline; up to three units may be taken in a studio course. The 18 units are recorded as choose_units 18 on the main list; the studio block has no minimum (it is optional, capped at 3 units counting toward the 18).","where":"Moreno Valley College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"The catalog prints no units beside any course; all units fields are null.","where":"Moreno Valley College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"Honors twins printed side by side in the comma lists (e.g., ART 6, ART 6H) are recorded as one entry with the honors course as an alternative.","where":"Moreno Valley College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"Catalog prints codes with a space (ARTH 3, ENGL 8, ETS 1, HIST 1, ENGL C1003, HIST C1001H, SPA 2H); the closed list stores them without a space (ARTH3, etc.); treated as the same courses.","where":"Moreno Valley College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"Catalog prints HIST 2, HIST 2H, HIST 28, HIST 29, HIST 44; the closed list has HIS 2, HIS 2H, HIS 28, HIS 29, HIS 44 (same numbers, subject HIS). Recorded as catalog additions as printed; a reviewer should check whether these are renamed codes of the same courses.","where":"Moreno Valley College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"The page states the Area of Emphasis lists cover all three district colleges and not all courses are offered at Moreno Valley College.","where":"Moreno Valley College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"Studio list note: ''some classes are less than 3 units''.","where":"Moreno Valley College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"Part 2: Rule: 18 units across three disciplines, 9 units in a single discipline, with a C or P grade. The discipline and single-discipline constraints cannot be expressed as blocks.","where":"Moreno Valley College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"Part 2: The ''Applicable Studio Courses Include:'' block allows up to three units toward the 18, a maximum rather than a minimum, so its minimum is left null.","where":"Moreno Valley College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"Part 2: The catalog prints no units beside any course, so units are null; the studio list notes some classes are less than 3 units.","where":"Moreno Valley College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"Part 2: Catalog additions in the studio list (DAN D19, ENGL 38A, ENGL 38B, ENGL 38C) are not part of this part''s course list and are not listed here; they should be checked in the other part.","where":"Moreno Valley College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"Part 2: History courses appear in the catalog as HIST codes (HIST 2, HIST 2H, HIST 28, HIST 29, HIST 44, HIST C1001, HIST C1002), while the closed list stores HIS 2, HIS 2H, HIS 28, HIS 29, HIS 44, HIS 6 and HIS 7. A reviewer should confirm these are the same courses under a renamed subject.","where":"Moreno Valley College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"Part 2: Careers come from the description: ''provides an excellent foundation for students interested in administration, communications, law, public service, and teaching.''","where":"Moreno Valley College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"Part 2: The catalog notes that not all courses are offered at all three district colleges.","where":"Moreno Valley College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"Part 2: No GE pattern is named; the degree references general education ''as described in the college catalog.''","where":"Moreno Valley College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"Read in 2 parts, because one reply could not hold the whole record.","where":"Moreno Valley College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"Reviewer: part 2 names blocks part 1 does not: ''Applicable Studio Courses Include:'' (kept beside ''Applicable Studio Courses Include'')","where":"Moreno Valley College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"}],"map":{"checked_run":"census-20261004T152834Z-s1of4","host":null,"status":"none","text":"The weekly census found no published term-by-term program map on Moreno Valley College''s site (census run census-20261004T152834Z-s1of4).","url":null},"v":1}'::jsonb from public.program_requirement_records r where r.college = 'Moreno Valley College' and r.control_number = '30169' on conflict (college, control_number) do update set display = excluded.display;
