er":"college","text":"The catalog prints HIST 44 for this program, and the state''s Program Course File carries it there: the program points at HIST 44 CCC000597002, Active in COCI.","where":"Norco College''s program record in the state''s curriculum inventory"},{"coci":[{"code":"DAN D19","current_ccn":null,"program_ccn":"CCC000520275","status":"Inactive"}],"kind":"Catalog and state file differ","owner":"college","text":"The catalog prints DAN D19 for this program, and the state''s Program Course File carries it there: the program points at DAN D19 CCC000520275, Inactive in COCI.","where":"Norco College''s program record in the state''s curriculum inventory"},{"kind":"Catalog and state file differ","owner":"college","text":"The catalog prints ARTH C1200, ENGL 48 for this program; the state''s Program Course File does not list them.","where":"Norco College''s program record in the state''s curriculum inventory"},{"kind":"Check not met","owner":"procedure","text":"The blocks add to 18 units; the catalog prints 18 units.","where":"Norco College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"The page prints two headings: ''Humanities, Philosophy & Arts - Associate of Arts Degree (AOE) - NAA497/C'' and ''Humanities, Philosophy & Arts - Associate of Arts Degree - NAA497/C''; both refer to the same A.A. degree (Area of Emphasis).","where":"Norco College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"Rule as printed: 18 units of study across three disciplines; 9 units must be taken in a single discipline; up to three units may be taken in a studio course; grade of C or better or P. The 18 units are recorded as minimum of the ''Included Disciplines and Courses'' block; the distribution rule (three disciplines, 9 units in one) cannot be expressed in blocks.","where":"Norco College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"The studio block is a cap (''Up to three units may be taken in a studio course''), not a minimum, so its minimum is null; studio units count toward the 18.","where":"Norco College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"The catalog prints no units beside any course, so all units fields are null.","where":"Norco College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"Honors twins printed side by side (e.g., ARA 11/ARA 11H, ART 6/ART 6H, HIST C1001/HIST C1001H) are recorded as one entry with the honors course as alternative; the catalog lists them as separate items in a comma list.","where":"Norco College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"Catalog prints HIST 2, HIST 2H, HIST 15, HIST 28, HIST 29, HIST 32, HIST 35, HIST 44, HIST C1001, HIST C1002; the closed list has HIS 2, HIS 2H, HIS 15, HIS 28, HIS 29, HIS 32, HIS 35, HIS 44, HIS 6, HIS 7, which appear to be the same courses under an older prefix. They are recorded as catalog additions by code; reviewer should check equivalence.","where":"Norco College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"ARTH C1100 and ARTH C1200 are not in the closed list (closed list has AHS 1, ARTH C1100H, ARTHC1200H).","where":"Norco College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"Closed-list codes stored without a space (e.g., ARTH4, ENGL23, HIST14, SPA2H, CHI11) are matched to the catalog''s spaced codes and not marked as additions.","where":"Norco College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"The page notes that not all courses are offered at all three district colleges.","where":"Norco College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"The degree requires general education but the text names no specific GE pattern.","where":"Norco College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"Part 2: The catalog prints no units beside any course; all course units are null.","where":"Norco College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"Part 2: Rule: 18 units across three disciplines, 9 units in a single discipline, with a grade of C or better or P. Recorded the Included Disciplines list as choose_units 18.","where":"Norco College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"Part 2: Studio courses may count for up to three units only; this is a maximum, not a minimum, so the studio block''s minimum is null. The catalog notes some studio classes are less than 3 units.","where":"Norco College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"Part 2: DAN D19 is printed in the studio Dance list (between DAN D13 and DAN D20) but is not in the closed list or in this part''s course list; it is not entered here and should be recorded as a catalog addition in the studio block.","where":"Norco College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"Part 2: The History list prints HIST codes (HIST 2, 2H, 15, 28, 29, 32, 35, 44) where the closed list stores HIS codes; reviewer should confirm these are the same courses under a renamed subject.","where":"Norco College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"Part 2: Careers are fields named as ''an excellent foundation for students interested in administration, communications, law, public service, and teaching.''","where":"Norco College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"Part 2: No specific GE pattern is named; the degree text refers only to general education as described in the college catalog.","where":"Norco College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"Part 2: This is an Area of Emphasis degree shared across district colleges; the catalog notes not all courses are offered at all three colleges.","where":"Norco College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"Read in 2 parts, because one reply could not hold the whole record.","where":"Norco College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"}],"map":{"checked_run":"census-20261004T152834Z-s1of4","host":null,"status":"none","text":"The weekly census found no published term-by-term program map on Norco College''s site (census run census-20261004T152834Z-s1of4).","url":null},"v":1}'::jsonb from public.program_requirement_records r where r.college = 'Norco College' and r.control_number = '30109' on conflict (college, control_number) do update set display = excluded.display;
