og and state file differ","owner":"college","text":"The catalog prints HIST 44 for this program, and the state''s Program Course File carries it there: the program points at HIST 44 CCC000597002, Active in COCI.","where":"Riverside City College''s program record in the state''s curriculum inventory"},{"coci":[{"code":"DAN D19","current_ccn":null,"program_ccn":"CCC000520275","status":"Inactive"}],"kind":"Catalog and state file differ","owner":"college","text":"The catalog prints DAN D19 for this program, and the state''s Program Course File carries it there: the program points at DAN D19 CCC000520275, Inactive in COCI.","where":"Riverside City College''s program record in the state''s curriculum inventory"},{"kind":"Check not met","owner":"procedure","text":"The blocks add to 18 units; the catalog prints 18 units.","where":"Riverside City College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"Rule as printed: 18 units of study across three disciplines; 9 units must be taken in a single discipline; up to three units may be taken in a studio course. The 18-unit choice is recorded on the ''Included Disciplines and Courses'' block; the studio block is optional with a cap of 3 units counting toward the 18, so its minimum is null.","where":"Riverside City College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"The catalog prints no units beside any course; all units fields are null.","where":"Riverside City College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"Honors twins printed consecutively (e.g., ARA 11/ARA 11H, ART 6/ART 6H, COMM 9/COMM 9H, SPA 2/SPA 2H) are recorded as alternatives of the base course; the catalog lists them as separate items in a comma list.","where":"Riverside City College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"The catalog uses subject HIST for History while the closed list uses HIS (HIS 1, HIS 2, HIS 2H, HIS 14, etc.); HIST numbered courses are marked catalog additions. Reviewer should check whether these correspond to the HIS courses.","where":"Riverside City College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"Closed-list codes stored without a space (ENGL8, ENGL23, HISTC1001H, SPA2H) were matched to the catalog''s ENGL 8, ENGL 23, HIST C1001H and SPA 2H.","where":"Riverside City College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"ARTH C1100, ARTH C1200, HIST C1001 and HIST C1002 (non-honors) are not in the closed list and are marked catalog additions; their honors versions are in the closed list.","where":"Riverside City College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"Careers taken from the description: ''provides an excellent foundation for students interested in administration, communications, law, public service, and teaching.''","where":"Riverside City College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"The catalog notes not all courses are offered at all three district colleges.","where":"Riverside City College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"Part 2: The rule is prose: 18 units across three disciplines, 9 units in a single discipline, up to three units may be from a studio course. Recorded as a choose_units block of 18 for the discipline list and a choose_units studio block with minimum null because the catalog sets only a maximum (up to 3 units), not a minimum.","where":"Riverside City College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"Part 2: The catalog prints no units beside any course; all units are null.","where":"Riverside City College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"Part 2: The discipline list prints history courses with subject HIST (HIST 1, HIST 2, HIST 2H, etc.) while the closed list stores HIS; these HIST entries are catalog additions and are not listed in this part because their codes are not among this part''s courses. Likewise DAN D19 in the studio list is a catalog addition not in the closed list and is not listed in this part.","where":"Riverside City College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"Part 2: The text says the degree includes general education but names no GE pattern.","where":"Riverside City College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"Part 2: Careers recorded from the description: ''provides an excellent foundation for students interested in administration, communications, law, public service, and teaching.''","where":"Riverside City College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"Part 2: The section notes not all courses are offered at all three district colleges.","where":"Riverside City College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"Read in 2 parts, because one reply could not hold the whole record.","where":"Riverside City College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"}],"map":{"checked_run":"census-20261004T152832Z-s4of4","host":null,"status":"none","text":"The weekly census found no published term-by-term program map on Riverside City College''s site (census run census-20261004T152832Z-s4of4).","url":null},"v":1}'::jsonb from public.program_requirement_records r where r.college = 'Riverside City College' and r.control_number = '18111' on conflict (college, control_number) do update set display = excluded.display;
