's CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"Elective Courses: ''Choose three courses from at least two areas'' (9.00-10.00). The areas are Area 1 History or Government (ETS-23/POLS-23, ETS-44/HIST-44, HIST-42), Area 2 Arts and Humanities (ARTH-12, ENGL-24, ETS-7, PHI-36), Area 3 Social Science (ETS-44/HIST-44, SOC-10/SOC-10H) and Area 4 Quantitative Reasoning and Research Methods (STAT-C1000/STAT-C1000H/PSYC-48/SOC-48). The at-least-two-areas constraint is not captured by the block structure.","where":"Riverside City College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"ETS-44/HIST-44 is listed under both Area 1 and Area 3. It is recorded once in the elective block.","where":"Riverside City College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"''Only one may be used'' groups are recorded as one entry with alternatives: ETS-23/POLS-23, ETS-44/HIST-44, SOC-10/SOC-10H, and STAT-C1000/STAT-C1000H/PSYC-48/SOC-48.","where":"Riverside City College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"The catalog prints HIST-42 and HIST-44, while the closed list has HIS 42 and HIS 44 with matching titles. They are treated as the same courses (catalog_addition false); a reviewer should confirm the subject abbreviation difference.","where":"Riverside City College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"SOC-48 (Statistics for the Behavioral Sciences, 4 units) is not on the closed list and is marked catalog_addition true.","where":"Riverside City College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"PSYC48 in the closed list has no stored units; the catalog prints 4.00 for PSYC-48.","where":"Riverside City College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"Th