e''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"Elective rule: ''Choose three courses from at least two areas'' (9.00-10.00 units). Recorded as one choose_courses block of 3. Area 1 - History or Government: ETS-2/HIST-31, ETS-14/HIST-14, ETS-15/HIST-15, ETS-21/POLS-21, ETS-23/POLS-23, ETS-28/HIST-28, ETS-29/HIST-29, ETS-44/HIST-44, HIST-16, HIST-17, HIST-25, HIST-32, HIST-33, HIST-42, POLS-20. Area 2 - Arts and Humanities: ARTH-9, ARTH-12, ENGL-18, ENGL-20, ENGL-24, ENGL-25, ETS-3, ETS-7, ETS-8, ETS-13/PHI-14, MUS-89/MUS-89H, PHI-19, SPA-12. Area 3 - Social Science: ANT-4/ETS-27, ETS-40, SOC-10/SOC-10H. Area 4 - Quantitative Reasoning and Research Methods: STAT-C1000/STAT-C1000H, PSYC-48, SOC-48.","where":"Riverside City College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"Area 4 prints ''Only one may be used'' above STAT-C1000, STAT-C1000H, PSYC-48 and SOC-48; it is ambiguous whether the restriction covers all four or only the STAT pair (PSYC-48/SOC-48 appear cross-listed). Recorded as one entry with three alternatives.","where":"Riverside City College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"''Only one may be used'' cross-listed pairs are recorded as one entry with the twin as an alternative.","where":"Riverside City College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"ETS-2/HIST-31, ETS-3 and ETS-7 appear both in the required ''Select one'' group and in the elective areas; presumably a course cannot count twice, but the text does not say so.","where":"Riverside City College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"ETS-21 and POLS-21 are marked ''( Historical )'' in the catalog.","where":"Riverside City College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"GE pattern: the section heading names CalGETC, but the closing paragraph still refers to IGETC or CSUGE requirements; reviewer should check.","where":"Riverside City College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"}],"map":{"checked_run":"census-20261004T152832Z-s4of4","host":null,"status":"none","text":"The weekly census found no published term-by-term program map on Riverside City College''s site (census run census-20261004T152832Z-s4of4).","url":null},"v":1}'::jsonb from public.program_requirement_records r where r.college = 'Riverside City College' and r.control_number = '44155' on conflict (college, control_number) do update set display = excluded.display;
