it elective block). Minimum left null because the catalog states a maximum, not a minimum.","where":"San Diego Miramar College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"The catalog titles PARA 100 ''Introduction to Law and Ethics'' while the closed list titles it ''Legal Procedures''; same code, recorded as a closed-list course.","where":"San Diego Miramar College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"PARA 270 is printed with 1.0-4.0 units; the closed list stores 1.","where":"San Diego Miramar College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"Careers left empty: the description names work settings (''law firms, corporations, and government agencies'') rather than job titles; the start of the description is cut off, so a reviewer may wish to check for career names there.","where":"San Diego Miramar College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"The text says 18 units in the major must be completed on Miramar''s campus and up to 12 credits may transfer from accredited paralegal institutions.","where":"San Diego Miramar College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"The course descriptions section is cut off at PARA 160.","where":"San Diego Miramar College''s CurriQunet META reading procedure"}],"map":{"checked_run":"program-sequence-ppm run 37197332656","host":"san-diego-miramar.programmapper.com","status":"refused","text":"Miramar''s Program Pathways Mapper, linked from sdmiramar.edu/program-mapper, answered all seven of the reader''s requests 403 Forbidden on 2026-10-04 (sequence run 37197332656), and the 17 other mapper hosts probed that day did the same: the refusal is the mapper service''s. The pilot''s sequence for Fire Technology A.S. (05100) is not yet read. The reader keeps its name and never retries a refusal another way. It looks for the sequence on the college''s own pages and in its catalog, and asks this host''s front page once a run whether it has opened (Sam, open-asks sheet 29 card 3, 2026-10-04).","url":null},"v":1}'::jsonb from public.program_requirement_records r where r.college = 'San Diego Miramar College' and r.control_number = '22280' on conflict (college, control_number) do update set display = excluded.display;
